<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.8: Lesson Synthesis</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00259</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.8: Lesson Synthesis</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9b4a24c8-92d5-4169-94db-7f0a38af09d8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>The focus of the lesson is methods for writing equations of a line. The method you use is based on the information you are given.</para>
<para>The table can be used as a reference to write the equation of a line, based on the information given.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
    <caption>To Write an Equation of a Line</caption>
    <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>If give \(n\):</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Use:</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Form:</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Steps</emphasis></entry></row>
    </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>Slope and \( y \)-intercept</entry>
      <entry>slope-intercept</entry>
      <entry>\( y = mx + b \)</entry>
      <entry>Substitute the slope for \(m\) and the \(y\)-intercept for \( b \) into the slope-intercept form.</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>Slope and a point</entry>
      <entry>point-slope</entry>
      <entry>\( y - y_1 = m(x - x_1) \)</entry>
      <entry>Substitute the slope for \(m\), the \(x\)-value of the point for \( x_1 \), and the \(y\)-value of the point for \( y_1 \).</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>Two points</entry>
      <entry>point-slope</entry>
      <entry>\( y - y_1 = m(x - x_1) \)</entry>
      <entry>Use the slope formula \( m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \) to find the slope of the line. Then, substitute the slope for \(m\), the \( x \)-value of one of the points for \( x_1 \), and the \(y\)-value of one of the point for \( y_1 \).</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para>Encourage students to check their equations by using a graphing calculator or Desmos. Tell students to look at the graph to make sure it goes through the given points.</para></section>
</content>
